  <!-- =================================================== agent middleware -->
  <section class="midw">
    <h3 class="mw-title">Agent middleware: the hard parts already run here</h3>
    <p class="mw-lede">
      Middleware is the layer beneath the agent: capabilities the platform runs, so every
      workspace has them from minute one.
    </p>

    <div class="mw-grid">
      <div class="mw-tabs" id="mwTabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Agent middleware">
        <button class="mw-tab on" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
          <span class="mw-t">Code sandbox</span>
          <span class="mw-d">Isolated containers for running code, created on demand.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
        <button class="mw-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          <span class="mw-t">Remote browser</span>
          <span class="mw-d">Browsers the agent drives, streamed to the user over WebRTC.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
        <button class="mw-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          <span class="mw-t">Agent-to-agent calls</span>
          <span class="mw-d">One workspace calls another; the platform routes and authorises it.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
        <button class="mw-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          <span class="mw-t">Cross-agent filesystem</span>
          <span class="mw-d">Permissioned directories that two workspaces can both mount.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
        <button class="mw-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          <span class="mw-t">Memory store</span>
          <span class="mw-d">Long-term memory stores, mounted into a workspace as a directory.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
        <button class="mw-tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
          <span class="mw-t">MCP connections</span>
          <span class="mw-d">Connect a server once; the platform attaches and refreshes the token.</span>
          <span class="mw-bar"><i></i></span>
        </button>
      </div>

